# Transient task definition rendered by scripts/ecs_deploy_and_diagnose.py on every
# deploy. It is a snapshot of live ECS state, never a source of truth — committing it
# is how stale configuration gets replayed over production.
task-def-rendered.json

# Local verification infrastructure (pre-launch verification pass).
#
# `staging/` holds the re-runnable verifiers the launch readiness report cites --
# verify_schema.py, rls_inventory.py, exposure_check.py, fk_typecheck.py,
# verify_live_trading_off.py, run_pg_lane.py, try_alembic_head.py, bootstrap_pg.py --
# which are small and worth keeping. What must never be committed is what they produce
# and what they download: PostgreSQL data directories, the Redis build, and run logs.
#
# POST_LAUNCH_IMPROVEMENTS.md item 12: anything here worth running regularly belongs in
# scripts/ and in CI rather than in a directory named staging.
staging/pgdata*/
staging/redis/
staging/*.log
staging/pg_dsn.txt

# HY-01: pytest junit-xml reports. 24 of these were committed -- 39.5 MB, every one a
# `<testsuites name="pytest tests">` dump from a historical full-regression run
# (fullreg_FULLREG_P7..P10, fullreg_FINAL, p11b*_diag/*). A test report is output: it
# describes a run that already happened, on a tree that has since moved on, and nothing in
# this repository reads one.
#
# Only the .xml shape is ignored wholesale, deliberately. A blanket `staging/*.txt` would
# be wrong: 1159 of the 1176 committed .txt files were likewise unreferenced probe output
# and were removed, but 17 are cited by name from tests and scripts (sweep_anon.txt,
# p10exch01_endpoints.txt, p11b22_entry_staged.txt and siblings), so the extension alone
# does not decide it. Same for .json -- 48 removed, 5 kept, including
# provisioning_snapshot.json, which DATABASE_PROVISIONING_RUNBOOK.md calls "the artefact".
staging/*.xml
